# What holds each territory against being taken, from the release's Biomes table.
#
# It was one everywhere, and the comment here said so. `P-253` gave jungle a nature of two,
# and territories 6 and 7 are the jungles - so this file's opening sentence became false
# without a line of it changing, which is what a scenario written as prose plus data does
# when only the data has a check on it. `the_forces_are_the_ones_the_release_gives_each
# _biome` reads the release now, so the next one fails here rather than reading wrongly.

set force 1 1
set force 2 1
set force 3 1
set force 4 1
set force 5 1
set force 6 2
set force 7 2
set force 8 1
set force 9 1
set force 10 1
set force 11 1
set force 12 1
